{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"illegible-principal-grayfox","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\nA clean local `rebar review-code` run emitted repeated `rebar.llm.structured` warnings: `parse_structured: multiple candidates validated ...; selecting the LAST`. For `CodeReviewBaseOutput`, `CodeReviewFindings`, and `VerificationOutput`, the logged first and last candidates were semantically identical, so the run passed but incurred ambiguous parsing and duplicate output/token cost. A tracker search found only closed historical tickets (`exultant-neofascist-bluegill`, `floaty-precious-rodent`) and no open bug owning the live warning. Discovered while verifying `treelike-unamusing-grosbeak`.\n\n## Reproduction\nRun an enabled local `rebar review-code` over a small committed diff with the configured Bedrock/Pydantic-AI runner and capture `rebar.llm.structured` warnings. The observed run emitted the warning for three output schemas while returning PASS.\n\n## Plan\nUse `rebar-debug` to prove whether duplication originates in model text, native structured-output envelopes, retry aggregation, or candidate extraction. Coordinate with RP-01 research (`sandstone-fiendish-auk`) before implementation; do not preempt that session’s structured-output design decisions. If changing candidate-selection semantics or provider behavior is required, return an evidence-backed decision brief for approval.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The duplicate-candidate mechanism is reproduced and proven at runtime with raw response boundaries captured safely.\n- [ ] Existing closed structured-output work and active RP-01 research are checked for overlap/dependency.\n- [ ] Identical duplicates are distinguished from conflicting valid candidates.\n- [ ] The warning is eliminated without weakening ambiguous-output detection or changing selection semantics without approval.\n- [ ] Focused structured-output and review gates pass.","id":"d74a-6a76-c846-4710","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["warning","llm","structured-output"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Structured LLM replies emit duplicate valid payload candidates"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786925673924915001,"uuid":"f1ba11b8-2d49-4cee-a771-5e22557eb54e"}